---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'Disclosure and editorial policy for KenAshe.ai: how AI assists the writing, who is accountable, how corrections work, and affiliate or sponsorship disclosures.';
const updated = 'September 4, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Disclosure', path: '/disclosure/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="page-mark" aria-hidden="true">// disclosure</p>
      <h1>Disclosure &amp; Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This is the most important trust page on the site, so I keep it specific: what is written
        by me, what is written by a machine I built, who is accountable, and how I handle money
        and corrections.
      </p>

      <h2>Two kinds of pages</h2>
      <p>
        The durable, first-party pages here are directed and edited by me: the homepage,
        <a href="/about/">About</a>, <a href="/building/">Building</a>, <a href="/writing/">Writing</a>, the topic hub
        introductions, and the <a href="/newsroom/">Newsroom</a>. Some Writing pieces are written
        entirely by me; others use AI assistance and are labeled on-page. When those pages say
        "I," that is me, and I am accountable for the claims.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/blog/">Digest</a> is different, and it is labeled as such. It is an
        autonomous publisher I built: it reads about 36 AI sources daily, selects and writes
        posts, reviews its own drafts against an editorial quality gate, and publishes the ones
        that pass. There is no human approval loop before publish. Every digest page carries a
        visible label saying so, with a link back here. The system itself is documented as a
        project at <a href="/building/autonomous-ai-blog/">Building: Autonomous AI Blog</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Accountability</h2>
      <p>
        The autonomous system is mine, so its output is mine to answer for. I monitor it through a
        daily digest and step in to fix, update, or remove anything that does not meet the bar. I
        am the publisher of everything on this domain, machine-written or not.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If something here is wrong, tell me at <a href="mailto:hello@kenashe.ai">hello@kenashe.ai</a>
        and I will correct or annotate it. I note meaningful corrections rather than quietly
        changing the record.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links and sponsorships</h2>
      <p>
        I work in affiliate marketing, so some outbound links on this site may be affiliate links,
        which means I may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. I sometimes receive free or
        discounted access to tools I write about. None of that changes what I choose to cover or
        what I say about it. Where a specific link or post is affiliate or sponsored, it is labeled
        close to the relevant place; this page is the standing policy behind those labels.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>
        My editorial judgment is separate from any commercial relationship. I would rather lose a
        commission than recommend something I do not believe in.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:hello@kenashe.ai">hello@kenashe.ai</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 0;
  }
  /* Let the copy span the full content width. */
  .prose {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .page-mark {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
